  "notes": [
    "The master key is a specification test key, not a real one: its bytes spell out what it is. Every epoch key, slot and padding leaf here follows from it, so the whole tree is reproducible. A real k_master never appears in this repository (INV-TREE-05).",
    "The anchor block is placeholders and visibly so: this epoch was built here and published nowhere, so there is no transaction, slot or receipt to name. A vector may not claim provenance it does not have, however much more concrete it would look — which is the defect E-14's fixture carried and D-140 records.",
    "`preimage_borsh` holds the 161-byte leaf preimage, and §1.3 puts the asset commitment at its bytes 8 to 39. INV-DISC-01 places it there and nowhere else, because the QP signature is over those bytes and a verifier cannot check it without them.",
    "The qualified person's key is RFC 8032 §7.1's published specification test key, not a real identity. Its private half is public, so every signature here is reproducible."
  ],
